The Digital Forensics Workshop is an analytical aid. Its outputs - including
but not limited to file type identifications, hash verification results,
parsed artefacts and their timestamps, recovered or extracted files, and the
results of write-protection tests - are not verified fact and are not legal or
professional advice of any kind. They must be independently validated by a
qualified examiner before being relied upon.

Its software write protection is not a hardware write blocker and is not a
substitute for one. For evidence that will be presented anywhere it matters,
use a hardware write blocker.
